// SEAL-SPEC §6 limit 3 (I-T5), as a CONTRACT: a seal does not disprove a race.
//
// Two callers reach the same register; one seals, one does not. The seal makes
// its OWN sequence indivisible and says nothing whatever about the other party,
// who is invisible to it. This compiles, and it must: the invariant is about what
// a seal guarantees, and pretending otherwise would be the tag sigil refuses to
// be. What the language cannot see, it does not claim.
fn guarded() {
    seal {
        rune bltsize: u16 at 0xDFF058 write;
        bltsize.write(64);
    }
}
fn unguarded() {
    rune bltsize: u16 at 0xDFF058 write;
    bltsize.write(128);
}
fn main() { guarded(); unguarded(); }
